{"answerArea":{"calculator":true,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"According to the Mean Value Theorem, there exists a number $c$ in the open interval $(3,11)$ such that $h'(c)$ is equal to the average rate of change of $h$ over the interval:\n\n$h'(c)=\\dfrac{h(11)-h(3)}{(11)-(3)}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"First, let's find that average rate of change:\n\n$\\dfrac{h(11)-h(3)}{(11)-(3)}=\\dfrac{6-2}{8}=\\blueD{\\dfrac{1}{2}}$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Now, let's differentiate $h$ and find the $x$-value for which $h'(x)=\\blueD{\\dfrac{1}{2}}$.\n\n$h'(x)=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x-2}}$ [[☃ explanation 1]]\n\nThe solution of $h'(x)=\\dfrac{1}{2}$ is $x=6$.  [[☃ explanation 2]]\n\n$x=6$ is indeed within the interval $(3,11)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\nh'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\sqrt{4x-8}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}(4x-8)^{\\large\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{2}(4x-8)^{\\large -\\frac{1}{2}}\\dfrac{d}{dx}(4x-8)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{4x-8}}(4)\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x-2}}\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}},"explanation 2":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\nh'(x)\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{2}\n\\\\\\\\\n\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x-2}}\u0026=\\dfrac{1}{2}\n\\\\\\\\\n\\sqrt{x-2}\u0026=2\n\\\\\\\\\n(\\sqrt{x-2})^2\u0026=2^2\n\\\\\\\\\nx-2\u0026=4\n\\\\\\\\\nx\u0026=6\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"In conclusion, $c=6$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"Let $h(x)=\\sqrt{4x-8}$ and let $c$ be the number that satisfies the Mean Value Theorem for $h$ on the interval $[3,11]$.\n\n**What is $c$ ?**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"content":"$3.5$","correct":false},{"content":"$6$","correct":true},{"content":"$8$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"content":"$9.5$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"countChoices":false,"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":false,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
